A||N||2||Cplensdorf||Trunk Solenoid Ground (?)||||1||
Z||000000||Cplensdorf||04-22-2001||02:56 PM||||OK....my trunk latch release solenoid just stopped working.  I have determined that the problem is that the solenoid has no ground.  If I pigtail off of the ground for the ajar switch, all works fine. How is the solenoid grounded?  Scematic shows a mounting ground.  How is this possible on the composite trunk? Is it only grounded when it is closed, through the body mounted latch?||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||04-22-2001||03:22 PM||||The solinoid is only grounded thru the latch ring when the lid is shut. Try adjusting the latch slightly.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cplensdorf||04-22-2001||05:06 PM||||Thank...BUT....I kinda figured this out myself....sometimes you just have to look for the simple things...ONE WORD OF CAUTION:  When you close the decklid be sure that nothing wraps around the latch (like a gym back shoulder strap)'cause the trunk solenoid will not work any longer.  This would not have been a major problem, but my key cylinder has also been 'frozen' for some time, hence no trunk access.  This did solve the other problem that has eluded me though.  The strap 'thickened' the post and demonstrated that my persistent ajar light really was the decklid even though the switch tested fine.  The switch is literally 'missed' when the deck closes on the worn post.  Thanks again....||||reg||1
